iewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321389" owner_email="scollyer@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" ref="refs/changes/89/321389/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I819eb1e9558a65fef5bd188c487115609da8ab92" commit="45fd08fe6013f89712db0c11485766ce62242943" commit_message="Build: Use ccache to speed up builds  This almost halves buildall times on my machine.  Aseda reminded me of ccache.  Signed-off-by: Anton Staaf &lt;robotboy@chromium.org&gt;  BRANCH=None BUG=None TEST=make buildall -j  Change-Id: I819eb1e9558a65fef5bd188c487115609da8ab92 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321911 Commit-Ready: Anton Staaf &lt;robotboy@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Anton Staaf &lt;robotboy@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321911" owner_email="robotboy@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/11/321911/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibb7f3e8a03a64760758ceb29b0ac742ad0c9f3db" commit="84aa8be6fa19f3eec80ec5221c07d4e983d82249" commit_message="Increase time allowed for servod to start in deployment_test.  Sometimes, the &quot;deployment_test&quot; script fails with &quot;Connection refused&quot; from the servo.  Looking at the logs, there doesn't seem to be anything wrong with the servo as such, but it's possible that we're not allowing servod enough time to get started.  This increases the time allowance from 4 seconds to 10 seconds.  BUG=chromium:577324 TEST=None  Change-Id: Ibb7f3e8a03a64760758ceb29b0ac742ad0c9f3db Reviewed-